# Git safety

The repository belongs to the operator. AI is a development tool only.

- Never add Cursor, Claude, Fable, OpenAI, or any AI agent as author, co-author, contributor, collaborator, maintainer, or owner.
- Never change Git username or email.
- Never push unless the operator explicitly asks.
- Never create a commit unless the operator explicitly asks.
- Before any requested commit: inspect `git status`, `git diff`, and `git diff --cached`.
- Never commit `.env`, secrets, keys, tokens, credentials, Cursor/AI memory, agent transcripts, caches, `node_modules`, `.venv`, `.next`, generated media, or temporary files.
- If a file may contain private Cursor/AI context, exclude it and report it.
